            <ArticleTitle>Two cases of the bronchial carcinoid tumors successfully treated with the parenchymal-sparing bronchoplastic resections.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E669-E673</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.21037/jtd.2017.06.141</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Carcinoid tumors account for 2% of primary lung tumors. We report two cases of the relatively young patients with typical and atypical carcinoid (AC) tumors that were managed successfully with a parenchymal-sparing bronchoplastic procedure.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
